WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.670
Even as a small kid, all you ever wanted was
to climb.

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:08.860
Your little toes dangle off the edge of the
wooden frame of your bunk bed.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:13.559
Your action figures are down below on the
carpet looking as small as ants.

00:00:13.559 --> 00:00:17.970
Seeing the world from this height is an adrenaline
rush like no other.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:22.780
But soon you outgrow your bunk bed, and you
return to the level the rest of the world

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.110
is living on.

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:28.860
To recapture the feeling, you ride your bike
to the park, where you climb the tallest slide

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:31.190
and sit perched at its peak.

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:33.550
The feeling of the bunk bed comes back to
you.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:38.470
Up here, you’re closer to the stars and
further from your homework.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:41.220
You think, “I’m never going back down.”

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:45.579
But soon, there is a line of children on the
slide’s ladder barking at you, calling you

00:00:45.579 --> 00:00:48.970
a scaredy-cat, telling you to hurry up already.

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:52.149
A hand presses into your back and pushes you
forward.

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:54.510
Your small body tumbles down the slide.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:57.040
Just like that, your feet are in the sand.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:01.870
You’re at the same altitude as everyone
else, no longer special in your elevation.

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:03.590
But you’re not done.

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:06.610
You’re determined to go elsewhere and upward.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:08.240
You start climbing trees.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:13.320
First, just small ones with bumpy bark for
your feet to use like rungs on a ladder.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:16.480
It feels good up there, but soon you notice
you’re not alone.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:19.580
You’re sharing space with squirrels and
caterpillars.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:24.500
It’s not that you’re afraid of these little
creatures, but you want to go to heights few

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:25.810
else ever had.

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:28.420
You move on to a larger tree.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:31.410
This one, you even need tools to climb.

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:34.510
You lasso a rope around a branch and pull
yourself up.

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:39.530
To get even higher, you wear wide-receiver
gloves banned by the NFL so that your hands

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:44.119
are sticky enough to grip even the smallest
protrusions of bark.

00:01:44.119 --> 00:01:45.160
Soon you reach the top.

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:50.700
Now at the highest sturdy branch of the largest
tree, you look down at the world and see it

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:55.740
in perfect order: you up here, them down there.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.120
It’s beautiful.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:58.120
But then a noise.

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:01.869
A noise too loud to have come from below.

00:02:01.869 --> 00:02:03.710
Next to you, you see a bird.

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:08.869
It smugly smirks at you and flaps its wings
and flies higher, one-upping your accomplishment.

00:02:08.869 --> 00:02:15.360
It lands on a tiny branch above you, reaching
the actual tippy top that you couldn’t reach.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.890
And it’s then you realize that the feeling
you’re chasing isn’t just so you can look

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:25.000
down on the earth and scoff, but so you can
look up at the world and wonder.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:30.349
So, you spend your life with your chin to
the sky, feet following your gaze.

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:35.000
Everything you do, every action you take,
is in the name of elevation.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.850
You choose a career in being a union lineman.

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:40.650
You work the night shifts, climbing up telephone
poles.

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:43.440
You’re happiest farthest from the ground.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:47.780
Every November, you vacation to New York,
where you run up the Empire State Building

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:49.900
just to taste new heights.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:52.410
You submit 86 flights.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:53.910
1,576 stairs.

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:59.390
But no matter what extremes you go to, you
feel like there is something up there still

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:01.780
out of reach, waiting for you.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:04.459
There is only one thing that will satisfy
you.

00:03:04.459 --> 00:03:05.459
Mt.

00:03:05.459 --> 00:03:06.459
Everest.

00:03:06.459 --> 00:03:11.300
If you can just reach the summit, you promise
yourself, your wife, your god, and your family

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:16.240
that you’ll stop straining your neck upward,
that you’ll enjoy what’s in plain sight,

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:21.110
that you’ll settle down and live the life
that’s right there in front you.

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:23.739
You begin to study for your two-month climb.

00:03:23.739 --> 00:03:26.180
You learn about the subzero temperatures.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:29.269
You learn about the journey’s physical demands
on your body.

00:03:29.269 --> 00:03:33.599
You learn about navigation, communication,
and preparation.

00:03:33.599 --> 00:03:39.300
But what you don’t learn about, or rather
can’t learn about, is the anomaly that awaits

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.300
you.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:46.209
Unfortunately, some lessons are omitted from
books, left to be learned only by experience…and

00:03:46.209 --> 00:03:52.010
by that time…I’m afraid it’ll be much
too late in the lecture to get a passing grade.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:55.090
The day comes, and you begin your mission
to the mountain’s peak.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:57.080
There’s something otherworldly about it.

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:01.220
The way you move up this mountain…it isn’t
just a matter of labor.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:04.099
There’s a spirituality within the journey.

00:04:04.099 --> 00:04:08.959
You feel as if you are floating, being pushed
toward the heavens by some generous being

00:04:08.959 --> 00:04:10.090
behind you.

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:13.170
But what is it that actually pushes you upward?

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:15.519
Could it be as simple an answer as willpower?

00:04:15.519 --> 00:04:16.519
Determination?

00:04:16.519 --> 00:04:17.519
Skill?

00:04:17.519 --> 00:04:18.519
No.

00:04:18.519 --> 00:04:20.039
You’ve felt those before.

00:04:20.039 --> 00:04:25.050
And while they have surely powered many men
to do great things, this force is different.

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:31.860
It is not so much that it is pushing you forward…it
is more like it is pulling you up…or rather…luring

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:33.339
you in.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:36.520
You’re amazed at how effortless the journey
is.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:39.589
At least, that is, up until now.

00:04:39.589 --> 00:04:44.869
Upon reaching the 8,000-meter mark, also known
as the “Death Zone,” you begin to feel

00:04:44.869 --> 00:04:45.999
uneasy.

00:04:45.999 --> 00:04:50.770
No longer is each step light and graceful,
now it feels like your boots are filled with

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:51.770
cement.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.330
You could swear your backpack is full of bricks.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:58.210
For a moment, you think you have lost your
beanie and gloves, because your ears and fingers

00:04:58.210 --> 00:04:59.520
are ice cold.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:02.669
The journey suddenly becomes long and grueling.

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:04.090
Dangerous and difficult.

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:07.599
You use every muscle in your body to climb
this thing.

00:05:07.599 --> 00:05:08.649
You have to.

00:05:08.649 --> 00:05:13.110
You use every bit of mental concentration
just to keep moving.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.110
You have to.

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:15.110
But why?

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:16.110
Why now?

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:18.710
Could it be as simple an answer as exhaustion?

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:19.999
Accumulated fatigue?

00:05:19.999 --> 00:05:21.159
How could it be?

00:05:21.159 --> 00:05:24.110
You’ve prepared as much as humanly possible.

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:26.539
Not just in your training, but in your life.

00:05:26.539 --> 00:05:32.449
You were meant for this moment, but now the
moment is refusing your embrace.

00:05:32.449 --> 00:05:35.749
Nothing you could have done could have prepared
you for this.

00:05:35.749 --> 00:05:38.569
An amorphous feeling settles in your gut.

00:05:38.569 --> 00:05:43.710
You don’t understand it entirely, but you
anticipate something bad is about to happen,

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:48.870
and it is at this moment that you wish you
wouldn’t have traveled alone.

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:53.099
You wish you had a partner to reassure you
that everything would be okay.

00:05:53.099 --> 00:05:56.779
You wish you had someone a few steps in front
encouraging you forward.

00:05:56.779 --> 00:05:59.069
You stop and stare ahead and imagine it.

00:05:59.069 --> 00:06:05.330
You imagine a friend to struggle with, to
laugh with, to succeed with.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.710
And then suddenly, you don’t have to imagine
any longer.

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:08.740
You see someone…

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:09.740
but how?

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:13.169
Last you heard, you were the only one to be
traveling this way.

00:06:13.169 --> 00:06:14.669
Could it be an illusion?

00:06:14.669 --> 00:06:18.999
You squint harder and harder trying to make
sense of what you’re actually seeing.

00:06:18.999 --> 00:06:19.999
A human.

00:06:19.999 --> 00:06:22.280
Or at least, a humanlike thing.

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:25.479
It is wearing all white mountaineering clothes
and boots.

00:06:25.479 --> 00:06:30.479
There is something about the clothes and boots
that makes you think they might not even be

00:06:30.479 --> 00:06:35.619
clothes or boots at all, but more like an
extension of flesh.

00:06:35.619 --> 00:06:40.479
Although they appear to be made of traditional
clothing materials, they seem to be one with

00:06:40.479 --> 00:06:41.719
the figure’s body.

00:06:41.719 --> 00:06:44.569
And the figure’s body seems to be one with
the mountain.

00:06:44.569 --> 00:06:50.310
While you are on a mountain thousands of miles
away from your family, this…thing is at

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:51.310
home.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.310
But what is it?

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:55.979
You squint through specs of snow splashing
across your vision.

00:06:55.979 --> 00:06:59.720
It seems about average human height and average
human weight.

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:02.119
Could it be simply an average-sized human?

00:07:02.119 --> 00:07:06.310
You want to make this conclusion with your
mind, but your eyes won’t let you.

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:09.740
At this distance, it is still just a figure.

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:15.779
But as he approaches you, and the possibility
of a companion sinks in, you become more optimistic,

00:07:15.779 --> 00:07:19.099
and you think maybe this figure can be a friend.

00:07:19.099 --> 00:07:24.520
Little do you know, you have just met a mountain
climbers’ biggest foe.

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:26.389
Meet SCP-1529.

00:07:26.389 --> 00:07:31.659
You notice its black goggles, and then, strangely
enough, you can’t stop noticing them.

00:07:31.659 --> 00:07:34.589
You find it impossible to break eye contact
with it.

00:07:34.589 --> 00:07:36.680
You are physically unable to turn away.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:40.999
Not only that, but you do not have any desire
to turn away either.

00:07:40.999 --> 00:07:43.689
You are drawn into its gaze.

00:07:43.689 --> 00:07:45.529
And you are happy to be there.

00:07:45.529 --> 00:07:50.789
For the first time in your entire life, you
are content with where you are at.

00:07:50.789 --> 00:07:52.830
You no longer care about climbing Mt.

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:53.830
Everest.

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:57.319
You strive no longer for great physical or
metaphorical heights.

00:07:57.319 --> 00:08:01.680
You are more than okay with where you are
at right here, right now.

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:07.490
And now you begin to feel very warm and comfortable,
and you have a sudden urge to sit down and

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:09.059
relax for a while.

00:08:09.059 --> 00:08:14.629
The unhurried pace of your movements matches
the stoned swaying seen at a reggae concert.

00:08:14.629 --> 00:08:16.840
You sit down and rock back and forth.

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:22.119
You are at peace in this idleness, almost
in a sedated state of consciousness.

00:08:22.119 --> 00:08:26.879
You misinterpret the signs of this dangerous
anomaly as a sign of personal growth.

00:08:26.879 --> 00:08:31.330
You believe wholeheartedly that this is who
you are now and that this is who you were

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:32.990
always meant to be.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:36.180
With newfound peace, you settle into the snow.

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:37.370
You embrace the moment.

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:40.740
And that’s when it gets even worse.

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:46.819
SCP-1529 moves toward you, navigating the
mountain with ease, using just his hands and

00:08:46.819 --> 00:08:48.760
feet, no gear needed.

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:52.449
As its arrival looms, there is nothing you
can do but wait.

00:08:52.449 --> 00:08:54.730
But what exactly are you waiting for?

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:56.410
What’s going on?

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:58.029
Where did this thing come from?

00:08:58.029 --> 00:09:00.769
Well, you wouldn’t be the first to ask.

00:09:00.769 --> 00:09:05.970
L, the subject of Incident 1529-1, questioned
this himself.

00:09:05.970 --> 00:09:11.250
L was reportedly killed during an encounter
with SCP-1529 when it abruptly became active

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:13.880
shortly after he had reached the mountain's
summit.

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:18.399
However, L was eventually found alive when
another team reached his position nearly two

00:09:18.399 --> 00:09:21.709
days later and removed him safely from the
mountain.

00:09:21.709 --> 00:09:26.350
He required fingertip and toe amputations
due to frostbite but otherwise made a full

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:27.350
recovery.

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:32.000
While still in the hospital, an agent of The
Foundation was able to ask him questions and

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.279
figure out what he had experienced.

00:09:34.279 --> 00:09:39.089
It was a difficult time for L, but it was
an exciting time for The Foundation.

00:09:39.089 --> 00:09:44.129
From what they previously understood of SCP-1529,
they never thought they would ever hear the

00:09:44.129 --> 00:09:46.710
truth straight from its victim’s mouth.

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:50.220
Until then, it was only ever told through
their autopsy.

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:51.910
L was on his way down the mountain.

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:56.709
He was proud and excited having reached the
top and accomplished his life’s goal, but

00:09:56.709 --> 00:10:01.519
he understood the trek back was no easier,
and that if he didn’t stay focused, he would

00:10:01.519 --> 00:10:03.839
end up dead like so many others.

00:10:03.839 --> 00:10:06.839
He noticed his hood was off, and he stopped
to adjust it.

00:10:06.839 --> 00:10:07.839
No big deal.

00:10:07.839 --> 00:10:08.880
Just a quick fix.

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:12.170
Little did L know, it would lead to such hardships.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:17.339
During his wardrobe malfunction, his group
made their way about six meters ahead of him.

00:10:17.339 --> 00:10:23.839
And it was then, standing in his newfound
loneliness, that he saw SCP-1529 coming over

00:10:23.839 --> 00:10:24.850
the ridge.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.200
L was a jovial fellow.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:28.589
His impulse wasn’t to fear the figure.

00:10:28.589 --> 00:10:33.459
Instead, he shouted and waved, assuming the
figure to be another climber left behind by

00:10:33.459 --> 00:10:34.459
his mates.

00:10:34.459 --> 00:10:36.310
Suddenly, it looked right at him.

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:38.779
And that’s when it started to happen.

00:10:38.779 --> 00:10:40.470
L felt happy and relieved.

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:44.850
It was like all the pain and the soreness
and the chill were gone.

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:47.149
No longer did he have blisters on his feet.

00:10:47.149 --> 00:10:48.879
He could feel his toes again.

00:10:48.879 --> 00:10:51.850
It was like he was back home in front of the
fireplace.

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:56.339
It was as if the journey was complete, and
his efforts had been rewarded.

00:10:56.339 --> 00:10:58.810
L no longer minded the mission back down.

00:10:58.810 --> 00:11:01.210
He felt perfectly fine where he was.

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:05.810
But even still, while his body was content,
his gut didn’t trust the feeling.

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:06.910
Something was off.

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:10.079
Why would L go all this way only to become
complacent?

00:11:10.079 --> 00:11:11.709
He kept thinking.

00:11:11.709 --> 00:11:16.810
He kept fighting the urges to relax, to succumb
to supposed feelings of warmth.

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:20.089
He knew the stories of men who felt similar
misleading sensations.

00:11:20.089 --> 00:11:25.319
When your body starts to cool down to an extreme
degree, your blood vessels dilate, and you

00:11:25.319 --> 00:11:27.890
start to feel like you’re actually warming
up.

00:11:27.890 --> 00:11:31.280
In these instances, people often tear off
their clothes because they feel like they

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:33.639
are burning up and need to cool down.

00:11:33.639 --> 00:11:37.060
Next thing they know, they’re naked and
frozen to death.

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:39.220
L would not go like that.

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:40.690
He had too much pride.

00:11:40.690 --> 00:11:45.350
He tried to shrug off the feeling of warmth,
but before he even could…it was stripped

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:46.490
from him.

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:52.829
As SCP-1529 got closer, suddenly, all of the
heat and comfort L had experienced was gone.

00:11:52.829 --> 00:11:54.040
He was cold.

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:56.709
Colder than he had ever been before.

00:11:56.709 --> 00:11:59.390
His fingers and face no longer had feeling.

00:11:59.390 --> 00:12:01.959
His lips peeled, snapped, and cracked.

00:12:01.959 --> 00:12:03.160
They were frozen.

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:04.509
His legs cramped up.

00:12:04.509 --> 00:12:07.540
He buckled at the knees and dropped to the
snow.

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:13.310
He tried to yell for help, but all that came
out was a soft and pathetic whisper.

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:17.510
SCP-1529 grabbed L’s shoulders and pulled
him toward its face.

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:20.569
L looked into his goggles, having no other
choice.

00:12:20.569 --> 00:12:22.730
He saw images in the lenses.

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:27.730
And suddenly it was as if L was watching a
film, or rather brief vignettes.

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:30.060
He saw people in hot tubs relaxing.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:32.339
A woman curled up by an open fire.

00:12:32.339 --> 00:12:34.620
A couple sunbathing on the beach.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:37.630
L recognized all these warm and happy people.

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:43.060
They were people he had seen on the way up
the mountain but not the way down.

00:12:43.060 --> 00:12:48.860
It only took a moment for L to realize they
were people who had fallen to SCP-1529.

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:51.089
It was then that L knew he had to resist.

00:12:51.089 --> 00:12:55.430
But SCP-1529 doesn’t take well to defiance.

00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:58.819
The images in the goggles changed from happy
to horror.

00:12:58.819 --> 00:13:02.139
The same people were now laying in the snow,
half-dead.

00:13:02.139 --> 00:13:04.660
L couldn’t manage to look at it for another
second.

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:08.670
He balled his fist with whatever strength
God was willing to lend him, he tried to strike

00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:11.420
SCP-1529 in the goggles.

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:14.790
His arm moved slowly at first, like a punch
in a dream.

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:19.459
It was moving as if the air it traveled through
was thick Jell-O. Suddenly, it snapped into

00:13:19.459 --> 00:13:25.640
full speed and drilled SCP-1529 square in
the center of his goggles, ultimately leading

00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:27.029
to L’s rescue.

00:13:27.029 --> 00:13:29.269
But this is no princess movie.

00:13:29.269 --> 00:13:31.860
Not everyone is so lucky to be rescued.

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:34.279
This brings us back to you.

00:13:34.279 --> 00:13:35.279
Yes, you.

00:13:35.279 --> 00:13:40.709
Wait, you didn’t think that brief deviation
from 2nd person would last forever, did you?

00:13:40.709 --> 00:13:42.189
So, where were we?

00:13:42.189 --> 00:13:45.160
Or should I say, where were you?

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:46.459
Oh, yes.

00:13:46.459 --> 00:13:52.730
You’re sitting in the snow patiently waiting
for SCP-1529 to kill you.

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:57.160
And as you wait for its arrival, you think
back to the survival lessons that L taught

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:58.160
you.

00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:00.420
Now, you see why I suddenly changed to 3rd
person earlier?

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:01.741
You needed that information so you can call
back on it for your third and final act.

00:14:01.741 --> 00:14:02.741
Isn’t that nice?

00:14:02.741 --> 00:14:03.741
Psh, who says omniscient narrators can’t
also be benevolent?

00:14:03.741 --> 00:14:07.019
So, you’re thinking of L and how he punched
SCP-1529, and you’re thinking you’ll do

00:14:07.019 --> 00:14:08.019
the same.

00:14:08.019 --> 00:14:13.870
But what you can learn from L, so SCP-1529
may have learned as well.

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:17.980
Would such a threatening creature ever be
defeated in the same way twice?

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:22.829
You notice that its goggles have been repaired,
and you intend on cracking them open again

00:14:22.829 --> 00:14:23.959
like an egg.

00:14:23.959 --> 00:14:25.750
But your fist won’t close.

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:27.410
Your arm won’t raise.

00:14:27.410 --> 00:14:30.810
You keep trying to start up your strength
like an old pick-up truck.

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:31.810
Nothing.

00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:32.880
Your luck eludes you.

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:34.190
You feel helpless.

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:36.970
And so, you sit in the snow and wait.

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:42.380
You can’t ball up your fingers into fists,
but you can bring one palm to the other and

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:43.380
pray.

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:45.639
You pray for help from your god above.

00:14:45.639 --> 00:14:47.800
Your prayers, however, are misguided.

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:49.879
Yes, there is help above.

00:14:49.879 --> 00:14:54.420
But it’s not a god that’s watching over
you, but rather The Foundation’s aerial

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:55.420
surveillance.

00:14:55.420 --> 00:15:00.180
A well-oiled system of spyware born out of
necessity, designed after the incident known

00:15:00.180 --> 00:15:03.170
as SCP-1529-2.

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:10.130
SCP-1529-2 occurred when an agent, located
in a permanent facility in China, observed

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:15.499
SCP-1529 through a telescope while it was
active near the summit of the mountain.

00:15:15.499 --> 00:15:20.110
That day, SCP-1529 looked directly into the
telescope.

00:15:20.110 --> 00:15:26.190
The agent immediately reported symptoms consistent
with an SCP-1529 encounter and reported that

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:32.480
SCP-1529 had begun descending the mountain
in the direction of the permanent facility.

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:36.420
Similar to the stories on the mountain, the
agent, too, was unable to pull himself away

00:15:36.420 --> 00:15:38.070
from the telescope.

00:15:38.070 --> 00:15:44.250
After 17 minutes under the spell of SCP-1529,
he was rushed to the facility sickbay and

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:49.490
found to have signs of frostbite in the fingers
and toes, despite having remained indoors

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:51.480
for the duration of the encounter.

00:15:51.480 --> 00:15:55.670
The Foundation then had to rethink its approach
to surveilling SCP-1529.

00:15:55.670 --> 00:16:02.600
When SCP-1529 is active, surveillance is now
conducted by means of an automatic telescope

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:10.350
with a video feed playing at seven seconds
delay to avoid a repeat of Incident 1529-2.

00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:15.759
When necessary and safe, additional observation
is done by way of helicopter and airplane.

00:16:15.759 --> 00:16:21.129
Furthermore, the bodies of any hikers who
encounter SCP-1529 are removed from the mountain

00:16:21.129 --> 00:16:24.390
as soon as possible for autopsy and disposal.

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:30.449
The Foundation attributes all SCP-1529-related
casualties to natural causes relating to altitude

00:16:30.449 --> 00:16:32.470
sickness and hypothermia.

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:37.459
Any survivors or witnesses are debriefed and
administered a Class-B amnestic.

00:16:37.459 --> 00:16:44.149
And for even further safety measures, Mobile
Task Force Psi-29029, also known as "Alpine

00:16:44.149 --> 00:16:49.689
Echo", remains on standby at all times at
the Foundation monitoring station, in a pressurized

00:16:49.689 --> 00:16:54.509
environment acclimatized to 7,900 meters above
sea level.

00:16:54.509 --> 00:17:00.839
In the event that a recurrence of Incident
1529-1 occurs, Alpine Echo deploys to the

00:17:00.839 --> 00:17:02.290
mountain by helicopter.

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:06.270
And so, by the grace of The Foundation you
will be saved.

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:10.480
Although sitting helplessly in the snow you
may feel your current state of existence can

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:15.339
best be described by the phrase dead meat,
you are more than likely to be saved than

00:17:15.339 --> 00:17:16.449
slaughtered.

00:17:16.449 --> 00:17:19.250
Even still, there is no comfort in the future.

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:25.970
On the mountain, right here, right now, you
are looking up and locking eyes with SCP-1529.

00:17:25.970 --> 00:17:28.400
Your whole life has come to this moment.

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:32.420
All you ever wanted as a child was to climb
the highest heights.

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:36.179
Aspiring upward has brought you so many good
things.

00:17:36.179 --> 00:17:37.179
Adventures.

00:17:37.179 --> 00:17:38.679
Financial stability.

00:17:38.679 --> 00:17:39.760
Respect.

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:44.899
Everything you have in your life is from the
simple fact that you did not settle for what

00:17:44.899 --> 00:17:48.320
you had but strived for what was above you.

00:17:48.320 --> 00:17:52.740
But now, this same impulse has gotten you
in a world of trouble.

00:17:52.740 --> 00:17:57.070
Had you just looked at where you were instead
of where you wanted to be, you would have

00:17:57.070 --> 00:17:58.070
been okay.

00:17:58.070 --> 00:18:02.279
If you just felt the snow beneath your feet
you would have been okay.

00:18:02.279 --> 00:18:05.750
But instead, you looked up, how you always
did.

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:08.900
You looked up toward the goal and away from
the present.

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.690
And look where it has led you.

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:15.400
The message of this story is clear, but if
for some reason we resist the lesson passed

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:21.460
down from one generation of thinkers to the
next, SCP-1529 is out there, waiting for us

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:26.059
to turn over our shoulder and look back or
tilt our chin and look up.

00:18:26.059 --> 00:18:32.270
And at that point, it will force the moral
on you again, giving you no other option but

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:36.350
to experience its wrath: right here, right
now.

00:18:36.350 --> 00:18:42.760
Now go check out “Frozen Bodies on Everest
are ALIVE - SCP-5140” and “SCP-096 Killed

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:44.289
My Friend” for more high-altitude horrors!

